hey welcome to your new project camp  update so we bought this big piece of  land and are prototyping a more  sustainable way of living  not sure how it's going to go but let's  see and in the previous video you could  see  us while doing a lot of things really  and which means we have documented and  made a lot of videos  and videos is kind of essential for this  project because  99.9 of the people would never see this  place in real life  but they see it through a digital screen  so having good documentation and good  video  is crucial and i would say  it's been decreasing a little bit i've  gotten a bit more annoyed making videos  due to the camera i was using so i'm  going to show you  a new camera which i got we also have  two boxes to open up from people that  send some old camera gear  so we can have more angles as we work  but before we dive into the world of  cameras  uh we first need to help the neighbors  because they asked us to help out  harvesting some potatoes and they have  land  right here  [Music]  [Music]  so  [Music]  so  [Music]  how is it dave yeah it's good hard work  [Music]  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  [Applause]  buckets full of potatoes  [Music]  david  we just harvest all of the potatoes  which is  nearly not this way more  so antonio will take now to a place  where they stir them for the year  and we will have a little bushel which  is a little snack  nice how many kilograms potatoes did we  harvest  today we harvested about 600 kilos  in total this year they harvested about  1700 kilos  a lot of potatoes  [Music]  you  [Applause]  foreign  foreign  a new gift big gift  we have a lot of onion soup  all right so let's talk about cameras  here i have a new sony  zv1 yeah it's one of those small compact  cameras  apparently good for video taking and  vlogging on the go which i do a lot  someone donated from the community thank  you for that so we can upgrade our video  quality  i've actually been using it for the last  few videos some of you noticed that the  image quality got way better  no no one actually but i know and the  main reason to get it is actually not  per se the image quality but there are a  few  very annoying things about the camera  i'm currently using but let me change  them  alright so now you see the new camera  and here's the old one  it's a canon g7x mark iii  i used to have the mark ii which i liked  a lot and then i changed  to mark iii i never really liked it  there are a few things which are just  very annoying to me the main one  is that it should film in 4k but  actually it overheats after two minutes  the only moment that i didn't have any  problems was in siberia when it was -17  so we're currently halfway in the middle  of siberia  in time to get some fresh air  and it seems doable because it's cold  like really cold so the camera  was not overheating has a lot of  problems with autofocus so that's why a  lot of shots are often out of focus  this is also a known issue they even say  that out of focus on a previous model  was better  this is a bit of a detail but the main  reason i got this camera or upgraded  back then  was because you could add external audio  so you have an inlet to put your audio  jack  but it actually does have a mount where  you could slide in your microphone  so you have to buy this external thing  so you can slide in your microphone  kinda silly makes the camera much more  bulky  and recently the screen broke as you can  see here  not a big deal but sometimes the touch  doesn't work which doesn't help focusing  i started to notice that i got really  annoyed using that camera because it's  either not in focus or it overheats  especially when summer is coming so now  we have a new camera hopefully quality  goes up but also less frustration  during the filming process so you might  wonder if quality is important why not  use a dslr camera  i have one but to be honest i rarely use  it because  a lot of complex settings to get into it  takes more time t